{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"77852dfb44afb685442ef779e6886bcdf543ab717dacda1a3e3755433378c431","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_6d8fa5f4020b31f8e597ba1ce296c103d868ce45ae5d29907e61b4be9a7c6aa1","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a coherent and well-motivated extension of the probabilistic interpretation of CCA to deep generative models. The primary originality lies in the specific combination of variational inference with the CCA latent variable structure, which the authors clearly distinguish from multi-view autoencoders. The introduction of the VCCA-private variant to handle view-specific factors is a meaningful methodological addition that addresses a practical limitation of the base model. The experimental evaluation is grounded in established benchmarks, and the analysis of the learned representations provides useful insights into the model's behavior.","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_identity_sha256":"409c30d2e53e6d88a56200d7082f3e60f4a711ab8ea655fc658690592a4fe7ff","prompt_identity_sha256":"07d969fe5a53af1f486b5c7ae74f846dafb8bdf2e9e806434fefe6436967451a","raw_response_sha256":"c1a77497968875d80cc23795db82dc31ed07f879582fde0b60892ec3727180b9","request_identity_sha256":"8f465dbbd1f716135b3e388cd8359c5b0bfeacde0c03344fda73232bf8bb6395","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"b821e43be712e80f9ef8a1c1bd694e1cef6c4afedb10f9131936b7e1cfdffab5","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-019"],"review_text":"The paper does not introduce a fundamentally new problem or task, as multi-view representation learning is an established area. However, it identifies a specific gap in existing deep CCA methods: the loss of the generative probabilistic interpretation and the difficulty in optimizing constrained objectives. The formulation of VCCA as a deep generative model that extends the latent variable interpretation of linear CCA is a meaningful refinement of the problem setup, particularly in addressing the intractability of marginal likelihood and inference in nonlinear settings.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-PROB"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-010","SRC-020"],"review_text":"The paper introduces VCCA, a new algorithmic approach that parameterizes the observation models of the CCA latent variable model with deep neural networks. It derives a variational lower bound for the data likelihood, which is a distinct methodological contribution compared to the direct optimization of canonical correlation in DCCA. The VCCA-private variant further extends this by introducing view-specific latent variables, providing a more flexible generative model. The use of the reparameterization trick for efficient training is a standard technique but is effectively applied here to enable end-to-end optimization of the deep generative model.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-MTH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-018","SRC-035","SRC-038"],"review_text":"The paper provides a clear analysis of the relationship between VCCA and multi-view autoencoders (MVAE), showing that MVAE is a special case of VCCA where the posterior variance approaches zero. This analysis helps clarify the role of the KL divergence term and the sampling procedure in VCCA. Additionally, the paper offers insights into the disentanglement of shared and private variables in VCCA-private, using t-SNE visualizations to demonstrate that private variables capture style information while shared variables capture class information. These analyses deepen the understanding of how the model learns representations.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-ANL"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-030","SRC-039"],"review_text":"The experimental setup uses established datasets (Noisy MNIST, XRMB, MIR-Flickr) and standard evaluation protocols (linear SVM classification, phone error rate, mAP). While the datasets are not new, the application of the proposed VCCA and VCCA-private models to these tasks, particularly the comparison with DCCA, DCCAE, and MVAE, provides a useful benchmark for evaluating the effectiveness of the new generative approach. The creation of the Noisy MNIST dataset by adding rotation and noise to standard MNIST images is a minor but relevant adaptation to test the model's robustness and generative capabilities.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008","SRC-016","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper combines the latent variable model interpretation of CCA with variational inference and deep neural networks. This combination is presented as a novel way to retain the probabilistic structure of CCA while gaining the representational power of deep learning. The rationale for this combination is well-articulated, emphasizing the benefits of a generative model for multi-view learning, such as the ability to generate samples and the avoidance of optimization challenges associated with constrained objectives in DCCA. The combination of VCCA with private variables in VCCA-private is also a creative extension that addresses the limitation of assuming common variables are sufficient to generate the views.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-COM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not primarily focus on negative results or critical assessments of existing methods. While it mentions limitations of DCCA and DCCAE, such as the dominance of the canonical correlation term and optimization challenges, these are used to motivate the proposed method rather than to provide a systematic critical analysis or negative result. The ablations and comparisons are standard for evaluating the proposed model's performance and do not constitute a material negative result contribution.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-NEG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5ac293d7e9f479602713796c50e1026353753b05d16cae942b7c2b112f3de51f","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_ordinal":89,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"c1a77497968875d80cc23795db82dc31ed07f879582fde0b60892ec3727180b9","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"61d29b022ca236ef64d22e5e1274bd6990e6f6943fb1b8ba85788f38ebe9a7b4","request_identity_sha256":"8f465dbbd1f716135b3e388cd8359c5b0bfeacde0c03344fda73232bf8bb6395","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1169,"prompt_tokens":21379,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":22548},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"8f465dbbd1f716135b3e388cd8359c5b0bfeacde0c03344fda73232bf8bb6395","role":"ORIG","role_ordinal":3,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}